From fc93187180b4efc69c5b7f1bc513d627e8c063a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:33:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] infinity6c: opt-in encoder statistics from
 RSS_VENC_STATS

RSS_VENC_STATS=<seconds> (from /etc/default/raptor, which S31raptor
exports) logs one line per H.26x channel per window: frames, the
keyframes' share of the bytes, average and largest size and the QP range,
per frame type. The QP is MI's per-pack u8FrameQP (frameQual), which no
stream analyser off the camera can see. A channel with RcParam extras also
logs GetRcParam read back a window after the deferred apply.

It measures the I-frame share where the GOP-boundary burst is made, and it
is the instrument for testing the rate-control extras on a camera. Unset or
0 is off and costs one branch per frame.
---
 src/infinity6c/hal_encoder.c      | 134 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/infinity6c/infinity6c_state.h |  25 ++++++
 2 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

